# Who has to look at what before it merges.
#
# Ownership here is a review requirement, not a claim about who wrote something.
# The entries below are the paths where a change is disproportionately more
# dangerous than it looks in a diff.

* @batleforc

# ── Paths where a small diff can be a large change ───────────────────────────

# Credential handling, token verification and the sealed box. A one-character
# change in any of these is a security change.
/crates/notify-adapters/oidc/                 @batleforc
/crates/notify-adapters/sealed-box/           @batleforc
/crates/notify-app/src/auth.rs                @batleforc
/crates/notify-app/src/authz.rs               @batleforc
/crates/notify-app/src/keys.rs                @batleforc
/crates/notify-adapters/attachments-fs/src/token.rs  @batleforc

# The release pipeline and what it builds. Anything that can put bytes into a
# published image or a signed release is supply chain, whether or not it is code.
/.forgejo/workflows/                          @batleforc
/.github/workflows/                           @batleforc
/Containerfile                                @batleforc
/web/Containerfile                            @batleforc
/renovate.json                                @batleforc

# The suppression files. Each entry in these is an argument that something is not
# reachable; they are where a real finding would be quietest if it were waved
# through.
/.cargo/audit.toml                            @batleforc
/deny.toml                                    @batleforc
/.trivyignore                                 @batleforc
/.gitleaks.toml                               @batleforc
/charts/weebo-notify/.trivyignore             @batleforc
/SECURITY.md                                  @batleforc

# Translations, and the reason they are listed with the security-sensitive paths:
# reviewers read code diffs carefully and locale diffs quickly, which is exactly
# what makes a locale file an attractive place to hide markup. Components render
# these through `<i18n-t>` slots and `src/locales/locales.spec.ts` asserts the
# files contain no HTML — so this entry is the third layer, for the day a
# community translation arrives.
/web/src/locales/                             @batleforc

# Deployment defaults an operator inherits without reading.
/charts/weebo-notify/values.yaml              @batleforc
/charts/weebo-notify/examples/                @batleforc
/charts/weebo-notify/templates/networkpolicy.yaml  @batleforc
